'''Aspect of Solaris''' is a Pantheon [[aspect]] skill that grants a [[buff]] which inflicts Fire [[exposure]] on enemies within its radius, and periodically inflicts the stackable Sunscald debuff which increases the effect of exposure on affected enemies. Only one aspect skill can be active at a time.

==Mechanics==
This buff inflicts a base exposure effect of -10% to [[fire resistance]]. 

The Sunscald debuff has a base duration of 4 seconds and stacks up to 5 times, with each stack increasing exposure effect by 15%, or a total of 75% increased exposure effect on affected enemies. It is inflicted once every second; the interval cannot be modified. It affects all types of exposure applied by any skill or effect, not just the fire exposure from the skill.

Sunscald affects exposure including from sources other than Aspect of Solaris; for example, {{il|Scorching Ray}}'s -25% Fire Resistance exposure, {{il|Pyroclast Mine of Sabotage}}, and {{psl|Mastermind of Discord}}. In the case of Pyroclast Mine, the increased exposure effect is additive with [[aura]] effect from [[mine]]s.<ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/PathOfExileBuilds/comments/1v6wku8/all_of_the_new_pantheon_aspects/</ref> These effects apply before {{il|Eye of Malice}}.

Exposure effect is additive with the aura effect when used with {{il|Pyroclast Mine}}.

Aspect of Solaris cannot be supported by {{il|Enlighten Support}}.

==Acquisition==
Aspect of Solaris is obtained exclusively by using {{il|Brinehook's Ducat}} during [[Allflame crafting]], which adds {{ml|GrantsSolarisAspectCrafted}} to the item.

